 "title": "County Treasurer | luce-county",
 "text": "-->\nCounty Treasurer | luce-county\ntop of page\nSkip to Main Content\nHome\nCommissioners\nDepartments\nAnimal Shelter\nBuilding Department\nCounty Treasurer\nEqualization\nTownship Contact List\nZoning & Planning\nEmergency Services\nProsecutor\nCounty Clerk\nCircuit Court\nRegister of Deeds\nAmbulance Service\n92nd District Court\nSheriff's Department\nLCP and N. Manistique Lake Campground\nParks & Recreation\nProbate Court\nHuman Services\nMSU Extension\nEconomic Development\nFriend of the Court\nVeterans Services\nForms\nLinks\nFOIA\nSection Maps\nMore\nUse tab to navigate through the menu items.\nCounty Treasurer\nDepartment Functions/Services:\nThe County Treasurer's office is located in the Luce County Government Building. The primary goal of the office is to collect delinquent property taxes for the County of Luce. Through this office, the money is then invested in various forms to make additional operating capital for\nthe County.\nThe Treasurer's Office does accept partial payments on delinquent taxes in most situations. The deadline for redeeming delinquent taxes is two years. Property is sold by the State of Michigan at public auction approximately 2.5 years after it becomes delinquent. For more information regarding this procedure, please visit the State of Michigan website.The Treasurer's Office is also responsible for keeping permanent records of tax rolls, delinquent tax rolls, tax histories for various public agencies, and for banks, mortgage title companies and other interested parties at a nominal cost.\nOther functions include receiving County department deposits and making those deposits to various banks. They also certify that all taxes are current for recording of deeds. Dog licenses can also be purchased at the Treasurer's office.\nTreasurer Links\nCounty Treasurer Home\nLocal Unit Treasurer Info\nDog License Application\nForeclosure Information\nPlease reload\nCounty Treasurer:\nBelinda Bridges\nbbridges@lucecountymi.gov\nDeputy Treasurer:\nTreasurer's Office\n407 W. Harrie St.\nNewberry, MI 49868\nHours: Mon-Fri 8:00AM - 4:00PM\n(906) 293-8171 Phone\n(906) 293-3849 Fax\n© 2022 LUCE COUNTY MICHIGAN\nbottom of page",
